> After the martyrdom of St. Boniface, Vergilius was made Bishop of Salzburg (766 or 767) and lab[oured] successfully for the upbuilding of his diocese as[ well] as for the spread of the Faith in neighbouring heat[hen] countries, especially in Carinthia.[ He] died at Salzburg, 27 November, 789. In 1233[ he] was canonized by Gregory IX. His doctrine that the earth is a sphere was derived from the teaching of ancient geographers, and his belief in the existence of the antipodes was probably influenced by the accounts which the ancient Irish voyagers gave of their journeys. This, at least, is the opinion of Rettberg ("Kirchengesch. Deutschlands", II, 236).

